    "notes": "Q958585 and OSM way 238615551 identify the column. Eleven mapped parts give the plinth and shaft proportions, and the photograph with the Royal Castle behind the sculpture establishes the signed facing. The eleven mapped components set the principal proportions. The signed face and statue pose follow the exterior photographs. Fine facial features, heraldic relief and fabric folds are reconstructed approximations. The plaque lettering is represented by incised line fields. The Castle Square paving, surrounding buildings and underground routes stay in their native viewer layers. Physical-device timings are unmeasured. The procedural fallback draws the mapped capital as a detached slab."
